# 11. GRAY-OUT CARD RULE

When an objective ball is legally pocketed:

ONE corresponding card must become completed/gray.

Do NOT gray out every duplicate card.

Example:

Player has:

A♠
A♥
A♦
A♣
7♥
7♦
7♣

Player pockets Ball 1.

Only ONE Ace card becomes gray/completed.

The remaining Ace cards should remain visually available.

However, the objective Ball 1 itself is completed and does not need to be pocketed again.

This distinction is critical:

CARD DISPLAY STATE
≠
OBJECTIVE STATE

Maintain these separately.

